.\" Man page for the Improv CLI.
.TH IMPROV 1 "2025" "improv 0.1.0" "Improv Manual"
.SH NAME
improv \- headless multidimensional spreadsheet model CLI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B improv
.I command
.RI [ args ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B improv
is the command-line front-end to the Improv multidimensional spreadsheet.
It operates on a model store backed by an embedded (SQLite) Mentat datom
database. Each invocation opens the store, mutates the loaded model, and saves
it back.
.PP
A model is built from
.B categories
(dimensions such as Time or Product),
.B items
(members of a category, such as 2025 or WidgetA),
.B measures
(named variables indexed by a subset of the categories), and
.B input cells
(raw values at a coordinate). A coordinate maps category names to item names.
.PP
The
.B \-\-at
flag on
.B set
names a coordinate as a comma-separated list of
.IR Category = Item
pairs, resolved against the loaded model. Numeric ids are given directly on the
command line.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init \fI<db>\fR
Create or open the store at
.IR <db> ,
install the schema, and save an empty model. Use an empty string for an
in-memory database.
.TP
.B add-category \fI<db> <id> <name>\fR
Add a category (dimension).
.I <id>
is a number.
.TP
.B add-item \fI<db> <id> <category-id> <name>\fR
Add an item (a member of a category).
.I <id>
and
.I <category-id>
are numbers. The category must already exist.
.TP
.B add-measure \fI<db> <id> <name>\fR number|boolean|text\fR input\fR
Add an input measure.
.I <id>
is a number. The type keyword
.RB ( number ,
.BR boolean ,
or
.BR text )
declares how
.B set
parses values for this measure. The trailing
.B input
keyword is required; only input measures are supported.
.TP
.B set \fI<db> <measure-id> <value>\fR [\fB\-\-at\fR \fICat=Item,Cat=Item ...\fR]
Set an input cell. The
.I <value>
is parsed by the measure's declared type (a float for
.BR number ,
.B true
or
.B false
for
.BR boolean ,
verbatim text for
.BR text ).
.B \-\-at
maps category names to item names; omit it for a scalar cell.
.TP
.B list \fI<db>\fR
Print all categories, items, measures, and input cells.
.TP
.B show \fI<db> <measure-id>\fR
Print one measure and its input cells.
.TP
.B export \fI<db>\fR
Print the whole model as pretty-printed JSON.
.TP
.B help
Show usage. Also accepted as
.B \-\-help
and
.BR \-h .
.SH EXAMPLES
Build a small Time \(mu Product model:
.PP
.RS
.nf
improv init          model.db
improv add-category  model.db 1 Time
improv add-category  model.db 2 Product
improv add-item      model.db 10 1 2025
improv add-item      model.db 20 2 WidgetA
improv add-measure   model.db 100 Price    number input
improv add-measure   model.db 101 Quantity number input
improv set           model.db 100 10 --at Product=WidgetA
improv set           model.db 101 100 --at Time=2025,Product=WidgetA
improv list          model.db
improv show          model.db 100
improv export        model.db
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I <db>
The model store: a single SQLite file created and read by
.BR improv .
An empty string names an in-memory database that is discarded on exit.
.SH AUTHOR
Greg Burd <greg@burd.me>
